294
00:10:22,370 --> 00:10:24,654
Lowering the price means someone gets paid

295
00:10:24,654 --> 00:10:25,088
less,

296
00:10:25,088 --> 00:10:27,372
and each of them has every reason

297
00:10:27,372 --> 00:10:28,658
to fight it.

298
00:10:28,917 --> 00:10:31,655
So why do Americans pay so much

299
00:10:31,655 --> 00:10:33,077
for health care?

300
00:10:33,367 --> 00:10:35,158
Not because they go to the doctor

301
00:10:35,158 --> 00:10:35,877
more.

302
00:10:35,877 --> 00:10:37,227
They go less.

303
00:10:37,327 --> 00:10:39,692
They pay more for each visit,

304
00:10:39,692 --> 00:10:40,561
each scan,

305
00:10:40,561 --> 00:10:41,429
each pill,

306
00:10:41,429 --> 00:10:42,927
and each claim.

307
00:10:43,017 --> 00:10:45,354
Health care in America is not expensive

308
00:10:45,354 --> 00:10:47,707
because of how much care people get.

309
00:10:47,817 --> 00:10:50,735
It is expensive because of what each

310
00:10:50,735 --> 00:10:52,502
piece of care costs.

311
00:10:52,750 --> 00:10:55,241
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

312
00:10:55,241 --> 00:10:58,212
we follow the money behind another hidden

313
00:10:58,212 --> 00:11:00,640
link of the world economy.

314
00:11:00,880 --> 00:11:02,780
This is The Hidden Economics.
